# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Both already resolve an extensionless path to the matching
# directory's index.html; these make it explicit so the behaviour does not depend on a host
# default that could change.
#
# THE 404 NEEDS NO RULE EITHER. Both hosts serve /404.html for a path they cannot resolve,
# with a 404 status, as long as the file exists — which is why it is a rollup input and a
# prerender target rather than a route. See vite.config.ts and src/pages/NotFound.tsx.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO SPA FALLBACK HERE. A `/* /index.html 200` rule would answer every
# mistyped URL — and each of these routes on any host that did not resolve it — with the
# LANDING PAGE and a success status: the wrong document, served successfully, which is the
# failure nobody reports.
/pricing   /pricing/index.html   200
/faq       /faq/index.html       200
/vs-cards  /vs-cards/index.html  200
/terms     /terms/index.html     200
/privacy   /privacy/index.html   200
